AltoStaking::lock()
├── given contract is paused
│   └── it should revert
├── given contract is in rescue mode
│   └── it should revert
├── given invalid inputs
│   ├── when sender is not authorized for onBehalf
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when onBehalf is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when amount is zero
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when container is deprecated
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when container does not exist
│   │   └── it should revert
│   └── when maxEpochsToLockFor is less than container duration
│       └── it should revert
└── given valid inputs
    ├── when position does not exist and isReuse is false
    │   ├── it should create new position
    │   ├── it should transfer tokens from sender
    │   ├── it should update container TVL
    │   ├── it should calculate expiry based on current container duration
    │   ├── it should emit LockPosition event with isReuse false
    │   └── it should return locked amount
    ├── when position exists and isReuse is false
    │   ├── it should update existing position with additional amount
    │   ├── it should transfer additional tokens from sender
    │   ├── it should remove old TVL from future epochs
    │   ├── it should add new TVL with total amount
    │   ├── it should update expiry timestamp
    │   ├── it should emit LockPosition event with isReuse false
    │   └── it should return total locked amount
    ├── when position exists and isReuse is true with matching amount
    │   ├── it should update position expiry without transferring tokens
    │   ├── it should remove old TVL from future epochs
    │   ├── it should add new TVL with same amount
    │   ├── it should update expiry timestamp
    │   ├── it should emit LockPosition event with isReuse true
    │   └── it should return locked amount
    ├── when position exists and isReuse is true with different amount
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when epoch needs to be advanced
    │   ├── it should advance epoch before processing
    │   ├── it should process position normally
    │   └── it should maintain correct TVL calculations
    ├── when maxEpochsToLockFor is zero
    │   ├── it should create position normally with full container duration
    │   └── it should not apply any epoch limit
    ├── when maxEpochsToLockFor is greater than container duration
    │   ├── it should create position normally with container's duration
    │   └── it should not limit the lock duration
    └── when maxEpochsToLockFor equals container duration
        ├── it should create position normally
        └── it should use the container's full duration 